what REDS %642, BOOKED, standing as queue item 1 on the eight-ship card: build the content-keyed scrub cache for the seed publish. The design that books it names its own falsifier -- if a measured publish spends its minutes somewhere other than the per-file scrub, the honest outcome is a page recording that with its numbers. The falsifier already fired once and nobody acted: the 20260916 timing paper reads the sed scrub at 15.92s of a 718.77s publish, 2.2 percent, while the witness runs a SECOND full projection at 354.09s and the copy loop costs about 131. Since that reading my own batched-classification lap cut roughly 215s of grep out of the projection, so every number on the card is stale in the direction that makes the cache worth even less. Re-run sow_phase_scan.sh --time on the post-batching tree, record the phases, and answer the falsifier in the design page and on the card rather than building a cache that buys seconds. No publish, no push to either public remote; custody gate 1 stays untouched.
